promptline (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Personalisation: promptline -P opens a file about your role, work,
    tools and environments. Command prediction and @agent both use it.
  * Permission modes for @agent (Preferences > Promptline): Ask (the
    default); Auto-review, where a reviewer model lets clearly safe commands
    run and asks for anything else; and Full, unlocked once promptline
    --guardrails holds at least three of your own rules. A built-in list of
    dangerous commands always asks, in every mode.
  * Every command the agent runs is logged to
    ~/.local/share/promptline/agent-audit.log, with how it was approved.
  * Memory: @agent remembers lasting facts about your work, learns from
    commands you edit, and forgets on request. Review it with
    promptline --memory.
  * @agent replies and auto-review's reasons print as they are written.

 -- Murcus Makhubele <murcus39@gmail.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:43:24 +0200

promptline (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix crashes when a shell exits in a tab, when splitting a pane inside
    a tab, and when closing a tab with its close button.
  * The mouse now works in the terminal: selecting, scrolling and the
    right-click menu (and so Preferences).
  * @agent commands get a real terminal: installer dialogs such as
    Wireshark's take arrow keys and Enter, and one Ctrl+C stops the command.
  * @agent works on a line recalled from history with the cursor at its
    start (zsh's history-beginning-search-backward), and uses the whole
    line wherever the cursor is.

 -- Murcus Makhubele <murcus39@gmail.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:05:34 +0200

promptline (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First Promptline release, based on Terminator 2.1.6: inline suggestions
    from history and paths, optional model-based command prediction, and
    @agent with per-command approval.

 -- Murcus Makhubele <murcus39@gmail.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
